## 1. Project Overview & Architecture

SkinTwin creates a persistent digital representation of an individual skin finding, updated through standardized photographs and longitudinal observable-change tracking. 

The workspace is organized into clean, independent directories:

```text
untitled/
├── frontend/                     # Flutter Web & Mobile application (Port 8082)
│   ├── lib/                      # Flutter UI screens, state, models
│   ├── android/                  # Android native project
│   ├── web/                      # Web entry point
│   ├── pubspec.yaml              # Dart dependencies
│   └── ...
│
├── backend/                      # FastAPI Python Application (Port 8000)
│   ├── app/
│   │   ├── main.py               # Application factory & middleware
│   │   ├── core/                 # Settings, security, errors
│   │   ├── database/             # SQLAlchemy engine & session
│   │   ├── models/               # Database ORM models
│   │   ├── schemas/              # Pydantic request/response schemas
│   │   ├── api/v1/               # Versioned route endpoints
│   │   ├── services/             # Business logic layer
│   │   └── dependencies/         # Auth & DB injection
│   ├── alembic/                  # Database migration scripts
│   ├── tests/                    # Automated pytest suite
│   ├── requirements.txt          # Python dependencies
│   ├── .env                      # Local environment configuration
│   └── alembic.ini               # Migration configuration
│
└── skintwin_ai_build_docs/       # AI & Clinical Architecture Specs
```

