## 3. Database Schema & Tables

All tables were modeled in SQLAlchemy and migrated via Alembic (`alembic/versions/3707d49db3c9_initial_tables.py`).

### 1. `users` Table
Stores registered accounts:
- `id` (String UUID, Primary Key)
- `email` (String 255, Unique, Indexed)
- `password_hash` (String 255, Bcrypt hashed)
- `full_name` (String 255, Nullable)
- `is_active` (Boolean, default `True`)
- `account_status` (String 50, default `"active"`)
- `created_at` (DateTime with timezone)
- `updated_at` (DateTime with timezone)
- `last_login_at` (DateTime with timezone, Nullable)

### 2. `skintwins` Table
Stores individual persistent digital skin findings:
- `id` (String UUID, Primary Key)
- `user_id` (ForeignKey `users.id` with CASCADE delete)
- `public_id` (String 64, Unique, e.g. `st-xxxx`)
- `name` (String 150)
- `body_location` (String 100)
- `body_side` (String 50, e.g. `"left"`, `"right"`)
- `description` (Text, Nullable)
- `status` (String 50, default `"active"`)
- `baseline_capture_id` (String UUID, Nullable)
- `created_at`, `updated_at`, `last_capture_at`

### 3. `captures` Table
Stores standardized photographs and imaging metadata:
- `id` (String UUID, Primary Key)
- `skintwin_id` (ForeignKey `skintwins.id` with CASCADE delete)
- `user_id` (ForeignKey `users.id` with CASCADE delete)
- `image_object_key` (String 500, private storage key)
- `image_hash` (String 64, SHA-256 integrity hash)
- `captured_at`, `uploaded_at`
- `quality_status` (String 50, default `"acceptable"`)
- `quality_score` (Float, Nullable)
- `reference_scale_available` (Boolean, default `False`)
- `measurement_status` (String 50, default `"unavailable"`)
- `device_metadata` (Text JSON)

### 4. `comparisons` Table
Tracks observable differences across pairs of captures:
- `id` (String UUID, Primary Key)
- `skintwin_id`, `user_id`
- `earlier_capture_id`, `latest_capture_id`
- `comparison_status` (e.g. `"completed"`)
- `alignment_status` (e.g. `"aligned"`)
- `reliability_status` (e.g. `"moderate"`)
- `observable_change_summary` (Text)

### 5. `notes` Table
Patient symptom entries and notes:
- `id`, `user_id`, `skintwin_id`, `capture_id`
- `note_text` (Text)
- `symptoms` (String 255)
- `created_at`, `updated_at`

### 6. `sharing_permissions` Table
Doctor / clinic access controls with revocation capability:
- `id`, `user_id`, `skintwin_id`
- `recipient_identifier` (String 255)
- `permission_level` (String 50, default `"view"`)
- `expiry_time`, `revoked_time`

